# course-discovery Python 3.13 runtime dependencies (phase 2, S2.1)
# Versions from docs/py313/course-discovery-py313-upgrade-2026-11-13.md §2.1/§2.2.
# Removed vs base.txt: boto, django-choices, django-haystack, django-storages,
# djangorestframework-jwt, drf-haystack, elasticsearch.
#
# mysqlclient lives here (not in production.in) because
# `course_discovery/settings/py313.py` is MySQL-only — unlike the upstream
# `local.py`, which defaults to SQLite. Without it every `manage.py` command
# under py313 settings dies with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'MySQLdb'`.
# It has no Python dependencies, so it stays a single leaf entry in the locks.
#
# pymemcache follows the same reasoning: `py313.py` selects
# `django.core.cache.backends.memcached.PyMemcacheCache`, whereas the upstream
# `local.py` used `LocMemCache`. Django builds the cache backend lazily, so a
# missing pymemcache only surfaces on the first cache access (e.g. the first
# `manage.py migrate` after any session/cache touch) — not at import time.
# Also zero-dependency.

